  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Jeremiah",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 13,
    "summary": "Israel and Judah will be as a rotted and decayed belt—The people are commanded to repent—Judah will be taken captive and scattered as stubble.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Thus saith the Lord unto me, Go and get thee a linen girdle, and put it upon thy loins, and put it not in water.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:1",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "So I got a girdle according to the word of the Lord, and put it on my loins.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 63
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:2",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And the word of the Lord came unto me the second time, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:3",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Take the girdle that thou hast got, which is upon thy loins, and arise, go to Euphrates, and hide it there in a hole of the rock.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:4",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "So I went, and hid it by Euphrates, as the Lord commanded me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:5",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass after many days, that the Lord said unto me, Arise, go to Euphrates, and take the girdle from thence, which I commanded thee to hide there.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:6",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Then I went to Euphrates, and digged, and took the girdle from the place where I had hid it: and, behold, the girdle was marred, it was profitable for nothing.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:7",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Then the word of the Lord came unto me, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:8",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Thus saith the Lord, After this manner will I mar the pride of Judah, and the great pride of Jerusalem.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "TG Pride."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Pride.",
            "prettyString": "TG Pride",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Pride",
                "entryId": "tg-pride",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:9",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "This evil people, which refuse to hear my words, which walk in the imagination of their heart, and walk after other gods, to serve them, and to worship them, shall even be as this girdle, which is good for nothing.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 78,
            "text": "HEB stubbornness."
          },
          {
            "start": 99,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "TG Walking in Darkness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Walking in Darkness.",
            "prettyString": "TG Walking in Darkness",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Walking in Darkness",
                "entryId": "tg-walking-in-darkness",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:10",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "For as the girdle cleaveth to the loins of a man, so have I caused to cleave unto me the whole house of Israel and the whole house of Judah, saith the Lord; that they might be unto me for a people, and for a name, and for a praise, and for a glory: but they would not hear.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 268,
            "end": 272,
            "text": "1 Ne. 1:20."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Ne. 1:20.",
            "prettyString": "1 Nephi 1:20",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1nephi",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 1,
                    "end": 1,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 20,
                        "end": 20
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:11",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore thou shalt speak unto them this word; Thus saith the Lord God of Israel, Every bottle shall be filled with wine: and they shall say unto thee, Do we not certainly know that every bottle shall be filled with wine?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:12",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Then shalt thou say unto them, Thus saith the Lord, Behold, I will fill all the inhabitants of this land, even the kings that sit upon David’s throne, and the priests, and the prophets, and all the inhabitants of Jerusalem, with drunkenness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 229,
            "end": 240,
            "text": "Ezek. 23:33."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ezek. 23:33.",
            "prettyString": "Ezekiel 23:33",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "ezekiel",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 23,
                    "end": 23,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 33,
                        "end": 33
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:13",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And I will dash them one against another, even the fathers and the sons together, saith the Lord: I will not pity, nor spare, nor have mercy, but destroy them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 146,
            "end": 153,
            "text": "1 Ne. 1:13 (4–13); 2:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:14",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Hear ye, and give ear; be not proud: for the Lord hath spoken.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG Pride."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Pride.",
            "prettyString": "TG Pride",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Pride",
                "entryId": "tg-pride",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:15",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Give glory to the Lord your God, before he cause darkness, and before your feet stumble upon the dark mountains, and, while ye look for light, he turn it into the shadow of death, and make it gross darkness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "TG Darkness, Spiritual."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 180,
            "end": 183
          },
          {
            "start": 189,
            "end": 191
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Darkness, Spiritual.",
            "prettyString": "TG Darkness, Spiritual",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Darkness, Spiritual",
                "entryId": "tg-darkness-spiritual",
                "book": "",
