              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:16",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "But if ye will not hear it, my soul shall weep in secret places for your pride; and mine eye shall weep sore, and run down with tears, because the Lord’s flock is carried away captive.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 154,
            "end": 159,
            "text": "TG Church."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Church.",
            "prettyString": "TG Church",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Church",
                "entryId": "tg-church",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:17",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Say unto the king and to the queen, Humble yourselves, sit down: for your principalities shall come down, even the crown of your glory.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 110
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:18",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "The cities of the south shall be shut up, and none shall open them: Judah shall be carried away captive all of it, it shall be wholly carried away captive.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 24:14 (10–16); 25:11 (1–12); 2 Ne. 6:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:19",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Lift up your eyes, and behold them that come from the north: where is the flock that was given thee, thy beautiful flock?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 69
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 84
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:20",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "What wilt thou say when he shall punish thee? for thou hast taught them to be captains, and as chief over thee: shall not sorrows take thee, as a woman in travail?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 77
          },
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 91
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 13:21",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "And if thou say in thine heart, Wherefore come these things upon me? For the greatness of thine iniquity are thy skirts discovered, and thy heels made bare.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 113,
            "end": 119,
            "text": "Hosea 2:3."
          },
